---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import RecentWork from "../../components/RecentWork.astro";

import ShopifyPartner from "../../assets/shopify.svg";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Shopify Development, Design &amp; Integrations | Kelp"
  description="Custom Shopify themes, storefronts, and integrations for brands with complex catalogs, POS and inventory needs, and ambitious ecommerce goals."
  darkHeader={true}
>
  <article>
    <SimpleHero
      title="Shopify"
      description="We build high-performance, conversion-focused Shopify storefronts using both Liquid and Hydrogen. We’re Shopify experts — from theme development and app integration to fully headless builds."
      dark={true}
    />

    <section class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <div class="platform">
        <div class="platform-logo">
          <ShopifyPartner />
        </div>

        <div class="platform-text">
          <p>
            We design and build Shopify storefronts that are fast, scalable, and
            designed to convert. Whether you’re selling a single product or
            managing an enterprise-level catalog, Shopify is one of the most
            flexible commerce platforms available.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our team is experienced in building both traditional Liquid themes
            and advanced headless storefronts powered by Hydrogen. We've helped
            clients update their Shopify themes while maintaining custom
            features, building out brand new custom themes, or just general help
            with performance improvements.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="service-body">
      <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
        <h2>Where Teams Get Stuck</h2>
        <p>
          A growing Shopify store can become difficult to manage when catalog
          rules, theme changes, apps, and outside systems are added without a
          plan. The store may look polished while product data, inventory, and
          customer-specific terms are maintained through manual workarounds.
        </p>
        <h2>How We Fix It</h2>
        <p>
          We audit the storefront and operating workflow together. The solution
          may be a focused theme improvement, a custom Liquid build, an
          integration, or a Hydrogen storefront. We choose based on the shopper
          experience, internal ownership, performance, and long-term
          maintenance.
        </p>
        <h2>From Theme Work to Custom Storefronts</h2>
        <p>
          We can refine an existing theme, build a custom Liquid theme, or plan
          a Hydrogen storefront when the experience calls for it. The right
          approach depends on catalog complexity, content needs, integrations,
          and the cost of maintaining the build. We do not recommend headless
          commerce simply because it sounds advanced.
        </p>
        <h2>Integrations Deserve Their Own Plan</h2>
        <p>
          A store may need to exchange information with a POS, ERP, warehouse,
          shipping provider, CRM, or product information system. Before
          development, we map which system owns each record, how often data
          changes, and how exceptions appear to staff. For B2B or custom
          products, that plan may also cover customer-specific pricing,
          approvals, quotes, variants, and production details.
        </p>
        <h2>Design for Discovery and Conversion</h2>
        <p>
          Customers need accurate product details, useful categories, clear
          shipping and return information, and a smooth route to purchase.
          Search and AI shopping experiences also depend on the quality and
          consistency of that information. We build pages that help buyers make
          a decision and make the data behind those pages easier to maintain.
        </p>
        <p>
          See Kelp's published Shopify work and ecommerce development approach.
          If your Shopify store has grown more complex than its current setup
          can handle, tell us where the buying or operations flow breaks.
        </p>
        <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Shopify experience and theme review</li>
          <li>Custom Liquid or Hydrogen development when justified</li>
          <li>Catalog, B2B, POS, ERP, and inventory integration scoping</li>
          <li>Conversion and content improvements</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
        <p>
          Show us the tasks shoppers cannot complete and the updates your team
          repeats by hand. We can use those examples to identify the right
          development path.
        </p>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <h3>Is Hydrogen right for every Shopify store?</h3>
        <p>
          No. It can be useful for a distinct experience or technical
          requirement, but a well-built Liquid theme is often easier to maintain
          and fully sufficient.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
            Talk Through Your Project
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <RecentWork
      tag="90"
      limit={10}
      heading="Shopify Stores"
      description="<p>Here are a few of the Shopify builds we’ve launched — all optimized for performance, scalability, and sales.</p>"
    />
    <FeaturedArticles
      category="93"
      heading="Our Articles about Shopify"
      limit={3}
    />
  </article>
  <style lang="scss">
    .platform {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 2rem 6rem;
      margin: 1rem 0;
      padding: 4rem 0;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--teal);
      &:last-child {
        border-bottom: 0;
      }
      &-logo {
        flex: 0 1 220px;
        text-align: center;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 2rem;
        order: 2;
        @media (max-width: 767px) {
          margin: auto;
        }
      }
      &-text {
        flex: 1 1 500px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
